13	1016,697,1319,970	Fig. 13.	The Morning-Glory pod: a round, smooth pod with a short point on top, the calyx of narrow curling sepals spread beneath it on its stalk.
14	1337,721,1660,980	Fig. 14.	The same pod fully ripe and dry, splitting from the top into three pieces so that the dark seeds show within, above the calyx and a long curving stalk.
15	1082,1332,1200,1460	Fig. 15.	A single Morning-Glory seed, a little enlarged: a dark, blunt, wedge-shaped body with one flat face.
16	1266,1272,1426,1497	Fig. 16.	A seed cut through lengthwise and magnified, showing the embryo whole and flatwise inside, its seed-leaves crumpled and folded to save room.
17	1488,1272,1654,1504	Fig. 17.	A seed cut lengthwise the other way and magnified, showing only the thickness of the embryo edgewise, curled round and surrounded by the pulpy nourishing matter.
18	1147,1639,1338,1838	Fig. 18.	The embryo taken out whole and spread flat: two broad, lobed, crumpled seed-leaves side by side, with the little radicle hanging below.
19	1391,1579,1623,1836	Fig. 19.	The embryo with its two seed-leaves, c, c, pulled apart on the summit of the stemlet, and the radicle, r, pointing downward.
